Research Overview for "Measurements of Branching Fractions of $	au$ Lepton Decays with one or   more $K^{0}_{S}$":

We report measurements of branching fractions of $	au$ lepton decays to final states with a $K^{0}_{S}$ meson using a 669 fb$^{-1}$ data sample accumulated with the Belle detector at the KEKB asymmetric-energy $e^{+}e^{-}$ collider. The inclusive branching fraction is measured to be $\mathcal{B}(	au^{-} 	o K^{0}_{S}\ X^{-} 
u_{	au})=(9.15 \pm 0.01 \pm 0.15) 	imes 10^{-3}$, where $X^{-}$ can be anything; the exclusive branching fractions are $\mathcal{B}(	au^{-} 	o \pi^{-} K^{0}_{S} 
u_{	au}) = (4.16 \pm 0.01 \pm 0.08) 	imes 10^{-3}$, $\mathcal{B}(	au^{-} 	o K^{-} K^{0}_{S} 
u_{	au}) = (7.40 \pm 0.07 \pm 0.27) 	imes 10^{-4}$, $\mathcal{B}(	au^{-} 	o \pi^{-} K^{0}_{S} \pi^{0} 
u_{	au}) = (1.93 \pm 0.02 \pm 0.07) 	imes 10^{-3}$, $\mathcal{B}(	au^{-} 	o K^{-} K^{0}_{S} \pi^{0} 
u_{	au}) = (7.48 \pm 0.10 \pm 0.37)	imes 10^{-4}$, $\mathcal{B}(	au^{-} 	o \pi^{-} K^{0}_{S} K^{0}_{S} 
u_{	au}) = (2.33 \pm 0.03 \pm 0.09) 	imes 10^{-4}$, $\mathcal{B}(	au^{-} 	o \pi^{-} K^{0}_{S} K^{0}_{S} \pi^{0} 
u_{	au}) = (2.00 \pm 0.22 \pm 0.20) 	imes 10^{-5}$, where the first uncertainty is statistical and the second is systematic. For each mode, the accuracy is improved over that of pre-$B$-factory measurements by a factor ranging from five to ten. In $	au^{-} 	o \pi^{-} K^0_S K^0_S \pi^{0} 
u_{	au}$ decays, clear signals for the intermediate states $	au^{-} 	o \pi^- f_{1}(1285)
u_{	au}$ and $	au^{-} 	o K^{*-}K^{0}_{S} \pi^{0} 
u_{	au}$ are observed.

